        "id": 1002137
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T09:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could try to make this `ProviderTypeGen\u003cV\u003e`, with `std::cell::OnceCell\u003cProviderTypeData\u003e` for `Value\u003c\u0027v\u003e` and `Option\u003cProviderTypeData\u003e` for `FrozenValue`, then use `starlark_complex_values!(ProviderType)`.\n\nThe mutable cell is then only touched during single-threaded evaluation, while frozen instance construction reads a plain `Option`.\n\nWould that meet the performance goal?",
      "revId": "530087918c62b12600b751e9575d1498dc2dd75c",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4639a659_fa47ccbc",
